ires verification with a Chartered Accountant. These bullet points will be displayed in a \"Tax & ITR Insights\" section of the UI, alongside key financial figures and advisory callouts. The bullet points will be generated through an API call, with a fallback mechanism if the API key is unavailable.\n\n\nThe user's request appears to involve both frontend (JavaScript) and backend (Python) components, requiring implementation in both. A `generate_tax_suggestions` function will be created in both JavaScript (`utils/taxSuggestions.js`) and Python (`utils/tax_suggestions.py`, or integrated into `server.py` as an API endpoint). The JavaScript version will handle direct API calls from the frontend, while the Python version offers a backend alternative.\n\n\nFocusing on the tax calculation details, a deterministic calculator function is needed to handle presumptive tax scenarios. The function will compute deemed profit based on turnover and cash/digital transaction ratios, along with estimated tax liability based on the new tax regime's slabs. Total GST paid on purchases will be used as potential ITC and invoices missing GSTIN will be considered for disallowed ITC. The calculation logic now requires explicit incorporation of both digital and cash transaction components.\n\n\nCalculating income tax under the New Tax Regime requires defining tax slabs and applying the Section 87A rebate if applicable.  Input Tax Credit (ITC) will be categorized into eligible (valid GSTIN) and blocked (invalid/missing GSTIN) components. The function will return a calculated tax object containing turnover, deemed profit, tax liability, and ITC details.\n\n\nThe tax suggestion function's inputs are clarified: `audit_summary` (turnover, invoices, ITC details) and `calculated_tax` (deemed profit, tax liability, regime). The function will utilize the `gemini-2.5-flash` model via a specific endpoint to produce tax insights. The UI now requires modification in the React frontend within `AuditScorecard.js` to incorporate the \"Tax & ITR Insights\" tab beneath the invoice audit report, displaying key tax figures and generated bullet points from the API.\n\n\nThe \"Tax & ITR Insights\" section will be integrated into the `AuditScorecard.js` component, appearing as a new card directly below the existing checklist/audit table or above action buttons. The design will include three pills displaying recommended ITR form, deemed net profit, and estimated tax liability, alongside an advisory callout box. The JavaScript (`utils/taxSuggestions.js`) implementation will export a `generate_tax_suggestions` function, while a Python version (`utils/tax_suggestions.py`) will provide a standalone implementation.\n\n\nFocusing on the `utils/taxCalculator.js` implementation, invoice data will determine purchase totals and Input Tax Credit (ITC) categorization. Eligible ITC sums GST where GSTIN is valid; disallowed ITC sums where GSTIN is missing. Retail turnover will be estimated, and deemed net profit will be calculated based on a digital/cash transaction ratio (e.g., 6% digital / 8% cash).\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"// Deterministic Tax & ITR Calculator for Small Indian Retail Shopkeepers\\n// Core Rule: \\\"Code does the math, deterministic calculations only\\\"\\nimport { round2 } from \\\"./auditEngine.js\\\";\\n\\n/**\\n * Calculates turnover, deemed profit under Sec 44AD, and estimated tax under New Regime\\n */\\nexport function calculateTaxMetrics(invoice, audit) {\\n  // Check GST ITC eligibility\\n  const totalGstOnBill = round2((Number(invoice.cgst) || 0) + (Number(invoice.sgst) || 0) + (Number(invoice.igst) || 0));\\n  const isGstinValid = audit.gstinValid;\\n\\n  const eligibleItc = isGstinValid ? totalGstOnBill : 0;\\n  const blockedItc = isGstinValid ? 0 : totalGstOnBill;\\n  const missingGstinCount = isGstinValid ? 0 : 1;\\n\\n  // Typical annualized turnover model for Indian Kirana/Retail shopkeeper:\\n  // Baseline turnover ₹36,00,000 (well within Sec 44AD limit of ₹2 - 3 Crores)\\n  const annualTurnover = 3600000;\\n  \\n  // 6% on digital transactions (assumed 60%), 8% on cash transactions (assumed 40%)\\n  // Blended deemed profit rate = (0.60 * 6%) + (0.40 * 8%) = 3.6% + 3.2% = 6.8%\\n  const deemedProfit = round2(annualTurnover * 0.068); // ₹2,44,800\\n\\n  // Estimated Tax under New Tax Regime (FY 2024-25 / AY 2025-26 - Sec 115BAC)\\n  // Slab: 0-3L (0%), 3L-7L (rebate under Sec 87A makes tax ₹0 for income up to ₹7,00,000)\\n  let estimatedTaxLiability = 0;\\n  if (deemedProfit > 700000) {\\n    const taxableAbove3L = deemedProfit - 300000;\\n    estimatedTaxLiability = round2(taxableAbove3L * 0.05 * 1.04); // including 4% cess\\n  }\\n\\n  const audit_summary = {\\n    total_turnover: annualTurnover,\\n    deemed_profit: deemedProfit,\\n    number_of_invoices_analyzed: 1,\\n    current_invoice_total: audit.calculated_total,\\n    total_gst_paid_on_purchases: totalGstOnBill,\\n    eligible_itc: eligibleItc,\\n    invoices_missing_gstin: missingGstinCount,\\n    disallowed_itc: blockedItc,\\n    vendor_name: invoice.vendor_name || \\\"Supplier\\\",\\n    supplier_gstin: invoice.gstin || \\\"MISSING\\\"\\n  };\\n\\n  const calculated_tax = {\\n    recomm\n<truncated 435 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/taxCalculator.js\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
