{"step_index":100,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T13:59:13Z","input_tokens":3223,"cache_read_tokens":96321,"output_tokens":1119,"content":"### Implementation Complete\n\nWe have created the function `generate_tax_suggestions(audit_summary, calculated_tax)` powered by **Gemini 2.5 Flash** and integrated the **Tax & ITR Insights** card right below the invoice audit report.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The `generate_tax_suggestions` Function\n\nThe function is available in both **JavaScript** for the frontend ([`utils/taxSuggestions.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/taxSuggestions.js)) and **Python** ([`utils/tax_suggestions.py`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/tax_suggestions.py)).\n\n#### Python Implementation ([`utils/tax_suggestions.py`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/tax_suggestions.py))\n```python\ndef generate_tax_suggestions(audit_summary: dict, calculated_tax: dict, api_key: str = None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generate tax preparation suggestions for small Indian retail shopkeepers using Gemini 2.5 Flash.\n    Input Context:\n      - Total turnover and deemed profit (calculated by code)\n      - Number of invoices analyzed\n      - Total GST paid on purchases (potential ITC)\n      - Invoices missing GSTIN (disallowed ITC)\n    \"\"\"\n    ...\n```\n\n#### Exact Prompt Used:\n```text\nYou are a tax preparation assistant for small Indian retail shopkeepers.\nGiven this pre-calculated financial data:\n{data}\n\nProvide 3 concise bullet points:\n1. Recommended ITR Form: (e.g., ITR-4 Sugam under Sec 44AD vs ITR-3) with a 1-sentence reason.\n2. GST ITC Opportunity / Risk: Explain how much Input Tax Credit can be claimed from audited bills and warn about unverified supplier GSTINs.\n3. Advance Tax & Action Item: Remind them of the March 15 advance tax deadline.\n\nTone: Grounded, simple English, no complex jargon. Include a clear disclaimer: 'Not tax advice; verify with your CA.'\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. UI Dashboard Addition: \"Tax & ITR Insights\"\n\nIn [`AuditScorecard.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/components/AuditScorecard.js), right below the itemized invoice audit table and compliance checks, we added the **Tax & ITR Insights** card:\n\n1. **Pill 1:** `Recommended Form: ITR-4 (Presumptive Scheme - Sec 44AD)`\n2. **Pill 2:** `Deemed Net Profit: ₹2,44,800.00 (Calculated at 6% digital / 8% cash)`\n3. **Pill 3:** `Estimated Tax Liability: ₹0.00 (Computed via New Regime - Sec 115BAC / 87A)`\n4. **Advisory Callout Box:**\n   > *\"Every rupee of GST shown on your purchase invoices can directly offset your GST tax liability via **Input Tax Credit (ITC)**. However, Indian tax laws (Section 16 of the CGST Act) mandate that ITC is strictly disallowed if your supplier does not have an active, verified GSTIN. Always verify supplier GSTINs on AUDIT IT before making payments to protect your ITC and avoid paying tax twice!\"*\n5. **Gemini 2.5 Flash 3-Bullet Summary & Action Item:**\n   - **Bullet 1 (ITR Form):** Recommends ITR-4 Sugam under Section 44AD presumptive scheme without maintaining bulky account books.\n   - **Bullet 2 (GST ITC Opportunity/Risk):** Dynamically informs how much ITC is eligible vs disallowed based on whether the supplier's GSTIN is valid (e.g. alerts when GSTIN is missing on Sample 3).\n   - **Bullet 3 (Advance Tax):** Reminds the shopkeeper to pay 100% of their advance tax by the **March 15 deadline** to prevent penal interest under Section 234B/234C.\n   - **Disclaimer:** *\"⚖️ Not tax advice; verify with your CA.\"*\n\n---\n\n### 3. Verification\n\nYou can test this in the running app at [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000):\n1. Select **Sample 1: Clean Bill** or **Sample 3: Missing GSTIN**.\n2. Scroll to the **Tax & ITR Insights** card below the line items table.\n3. Observe how Pill 1, Pill 2, Pill 3, and the advisory callout update dynamically based on the audited bill's GST status.\n4. Click **\"✨ Gemini 2.5 Flash\"** to re-trigger the AI recommendations on demand."}
