{"step_index":102,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T14:02:02Z","input_tokens":3254,"cache_read_tokens":97494,"output_tokens":3835,"thinking":"The objective is to enable real-time bill creation and calculation within the web application, incorporating both manual input and image-based uploads. This involves implementing an interactive bill editor and real-time upload functionality for existing bills.\n\n\nDeveloping real-time bill creation requires an interactive editor capable of handling manual input and image uploads, with fields for vendor details, GSTIN, invoice information, and line items. Real-time recalculations must occur with every input change, affecting item amounts, subtotals, and tax calculations, including CGST, SGST, IGST, discrepancies, and estimated profit/tax. The system needs to provide live updating visual invoice previews, discrepancy notes, and downloadable audit slips.\n\n\nInvoice rendering currently works, but direct bill editing capabilities are absent. The application needs features for direct input modifications like adding/removing line items, adjusting tax rates, and editing vendor details directly on the bill preview. A critical enhancement would be the ability to toggle between the rendered HTML bill and the original uploaded image, with interactive canvas overlays for image-based edits.\n\n\nReal-time bill functionality necessitates OCR integration for image uploads and a manual entry interface. Tesseract.js appears suitable for client-side OCR, allowing immediate text extraction from uploaded images. This will facilitate automatic bill parsing and field population, enhancing usability. The Gemini API can be integrated to refine image-to-JSON extractions when an API key is provided, improving accuracy.\n\n\nAdding a tax rate selector alongside manual CGST/SGST/IGST input enables flexible tax calculations. GSTIN input validation against the 15-character format, with visual feedback, will ensure data integrity. A \"Declared Grand Total\" input will allow for instant discrepancy checks against calculated totals.\n\n\nEnhanced file handling will store the uploaded image URL or Base64 data for toggling between the digitized invoice and original image in the `InvoiceViewer`. Client-side OCR parsing with Tesseract.js, using regex for extraction, will also be added.\n\nThe `InvoiceViewer` will support rendering the digitized invoice synced with inputs and the uploaded image with interactive bounding boxes and a toggle. The audit scorecard will switch from `change` to `input` events for instant recalculations, including add/remove item buttons, editable GSTIN/total inputs, tax rate presets, and state tax toggles. An auto-fix discrepancy button and a turnover/ratio slider are planned for tax insights.\n\n\nThe \"Share on WhatsApp\" and \"Manually Audit a Bill\" buttons will be integrated, and `annualTurnover` and `digitalPercent` in the tax calculator will be made configurable through UI inputs. The system will manage input focus in real-time, handling image URLs for custom uploads and facilitating blank bill creation. Input focus preservation is crucial for a smooth user experience; DOM re-renders should selectively update only the calculated fields, or the active element and cursor position should be restored post-render to avoid blurring and ensure smooth typing. The tax calculator component will be inspected to confirm the input enhancements.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"// Deterministic Tax & ITR Calculator for Small Indian Retail Shopkeepers\\n// Core Rule: \\\"Code does the math, deterministic calculations only\\\"\\nimport { round2 } from \\\"./auditEngine.js\\\";\\n\\n/**\\n * Calculates turnover, deemed profit under Sec 44AD, and estimated tax under New Regime\\n * @param {Object} invoice\\n * @param {Object} audit\\n * @param {Object} [settings] - Optional user overrides for turnover and digital ratio\\n */\\nexport function calculateTaxMetrics(invoice, audit, settings = {}) {\\n  const totalGstOnBill = round2((Number(invoice.cgst) || 0) + (Number(invoice.sgst) || 0) + (Number(invoice.igst) || 0));\\n  const isGstinValid = audit.gstinValid;\\n\\n  const eligibleItc = isGstinValid ? totalGstOnBill : 0;\\n  const blockedItc = isGstinValid ? 0 : totalGstOnBill;\\n  const missingGstinCount = isGstinValid ? 0 : 1;\\n\\n  // Annualized turnover: default to ₹36,00,000 or user slider value\\n  const annualTurnover = Number(settings.annualTurnover) || 3600000;\\n  \\n  // Digital vs Cash ratio: default 60% digital, 40% cash\\n  const digitalRatio = settings.digitalRatio !== undefined ? Number(settings.digitalRatio) : 0.60;\\n  const cashRatio = round2(1 - digitalRatio);\\n\\n  // Section 44AD Presumptive Profit: 6% for digital turnover, 8% for cash turnover\\n  const digitalProfit = (annualTurnover * digitalRatio) * 0.06;\\n  const cashProfit = (annualTurnover * cashRatio) * 0.08;\\n  const deemedProfit = round2(digitalProfit + cashProfit);\\n\\n  // Estimated Tax under New Tax Regime (Section 115BAC)\\n  // Slabs:\\n  // Up to ₹3,00,000: Nil\\n  // ₹3,00,001 to ₹6,00,000: 5%\\n  // ₹6,00,001 to ₹9,00,000: 10%\\n  // ₹9,00,001 to ₹12,00,000: 15%\\n  // ₹12,00,001 to ₹15,00,000: 20%\\n  // Above ₹15,00,000: 30%\\n  // Rebate under Section 87A: If total income <= ₹7,00,000, tax liability is ₹0.\\n  let baseTax = 0;\\n  if (deemedProfit > 700000) {\\n    if (deemedProfit <= 600000) {\\n      baseTax = (deemedProfit - 300000) * 0.05;\\n    } else if (deemedProfit <= 900000) {\\n      baseTax = 15000 + (deemedP\n<truncated 1612 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/taxCalculator.js\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
